# C# / Unity Standards

## Style
- Allman braces, 4 spaces; explicit types in public APIs, `var` for obvious right-hand sides.
- Naming: `*System` (implements `IEcsInitSystem`/`IEcsRunSystem`), plain-noun struct components (`*Ref` when wrapping a Unity object), `*Event` for one-tick events,
  `*View`/`*Marker` for MonoBehaviours, `*Config`/`*Settings` for ScriptableObjects, private fields `_camelCase`, `sealed` where there is no inheritance.
- Keep methods short; extract helpers past ~40-60 lines.

## Unity specifics
- No gameplay logic in `MonoBehaviour.Update`; the only `Update` users are `GameBootstrap` (drives systems) and `ClickRaycastToEcsEvent` (input bridge).
- Touch Unity objects from systems through view refs stored in components (`TransformRef`, `BlockViewRef`, `SlotView`, ...), as the existing systems do.
- Serialized tuning: `[SerializeField] private` + read-only property, `[Min]`/`[Range]`/`[Header]`; Luna-editable values get `[LunaPlaygroundField]`.

## Luna safety
- No reflection, async/await, threads, LINQ, `ref` returns or `foreach` over filters in runtime code; prefer `GetComponent<Transform>()` and the existing `InstantiateSafe` pattern.

## Error handling
- Validate config in `Init` (log with the system name and return); no exceptions in `Run`.
- Cache references once; no repeated provider/camera lookups per tick except where the existing code already does (`Camera.main` in block path code).
